  "changes": [
    "device_fops now routes open, release, read, write and ioctl through generation-checked wrappers. Wrappers take an atomic in-flight reference under the lifecycle mutex, release the mutex before calling the stock body, then drop the reference.",
    "Quiesce marks the cdev offline, advances the generation, wakes the TCM frame waitqueue, and waits for in-flight callbacks to leave. Both exact ioctl wait loops check the offline flag after joining the waitqueue and exit through the timeout cleanup path.",
    "syna_cdev_remove now quiesces callbacks and disconnects the device/IRQ before draining frame-list nodes and releasing cdev resources. Existing caller disconnects are idempotent because syna_dev_disconnect checks its connected state.",
    "Creation failure paths clear the cdev global state and invalidate the generation. Old file descriptors return -ENODEV for new data operations; stale release avoids dereferencing a retired TCM context."
  ],
